  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits a strong upward bias when the last historical price is near its local peak (e.g., >73), failing to account for immediate mean reversion.",
    "True outcomes show high volatility with frequent spikes followed by sharp drops, whereas model forecasts produce smooth, linearly increasing paths that miss these reversals.",
    "Sentiment history shows no predictive power; extreme sentiment values (+1.0/-1.0) do not correlate with subsequent price direction or magnitude.",
    "When the last 3 days show a downward trend (e.g., -2 to -4 points), the model incorrectly predicts continued growth, leading to significant overestimation.",
    "The model fails to capture the 'spike-and-fall' pattern where prices jump up by ~5-8 points then drop back down within the same 30-day horizon.",
    "Forecast errors are maximized in the first 10 days of the 30-day window, where the model's linear projection diverges most from the volatile true path."
  ]
}
